  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Top small-business government contractors listing for FY2027 to date shows contract obligations totaling $790M. THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC leads the ranking with obligations of $143M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC follows with obligations of $99.6M. IMPULSE SPACE, INC. appears third with obligations of $37.1M. BLUESTAQ LLC, METROIBR JV LLC, PRIMARY CARE SOLUTIONS INC, PINTER MEMORIALS INC, MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE, STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC, and A-TEAM SOLUTIONS LLC round out the top ten with obligations between $24.3M and $16.4M. The list reflects fiscal-year-to-date activity, so totals and positions are partial snapshots of FY2027 to date rather than full-year results. Procurement officers and contractors can use the ranking to see which small businesses have received the largest current-year contract obligations and to benchmark their own FY2027 to date performance against peers named on the list.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who occupies the top positions in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC occupies the top position with obligations of $143M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC occupies the second position with obligations of $99.6M. IMPULSE SPACE, INC. occupies the third position with obligations of $37.1M. BLUESTAQ LLC occupies the fourth position with obligations of $24.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the FY2027 to date total mean for small-business obligations?",
        "body": "The listing reports a cumulative FY2027 to date total of $790M in contract obligations. The total represents partial-year obligations, not final fiscal-year figures. Individual company obligations in the ranking contribute to that $790M total."
      }
